  :adr/body
  "# ADR-2607195700: Bounded PostgreSQL SCRAM-SHA-256 session component

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19

## Decision

The PostgreSQL `.kotoba` provider implements SSLRequest, verified TLS,
StartupMessage, AuthenticationSASL, SASLInitialResponse, server-first parsing,
client proof construction, SASLResponse, mandatory server-final signature
verification, bounded startup metadata and ReadyForQuery. Only
SCRAM-SHA-256 is admitted; mechanism downgrade, invalid nonce extension,
non-canonical base64, iteration values outside 4,096–1,000,000, malformed
frames and signature mismatch fail closed.

Production nonce input comes from the bounded `random_bytes` host primitive:
18 random bytes are encoded as a 24-byte SCRAM nonce. The deterministic nonce
entry remains for tests. Password material remains behind the purpose-bound
`secret/use-scram-sha256` capability and never enters component memory. Every
failed session closes its affine channel.

## Evidence boundary

The E2E test uses a real local socket and TLS handshake with a scripted server
that validates every PostgreSQL client frame and returns protocol-exact SCRAM
and startup messages. It proves component/linker/native-provider behavior but
is not yet an interoperability run against a released PostgreSQL server or an
external production PKI.

## Remaining maturity boundary

External PostgreSQL interoperability, channel binding/SCRAM-SHA-256-PLUS,
client certificates, cancellation, prepared statements, transaction policy,
credential rotation and production soak remain qualification gates."}]
